---
import Chapter from "../Chapter.astro";
import AccountCompare from "./AccountCompare.astro";
import "./bar.css";
---

<section class="section section-tint" id="bar" aria-labelledby="bar-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <Chapter numeral="II." kicker="Setting the bar" title="5× Outliers, or Min Views?" id="bar-title" />

    <div class="bar-intro">
      <div class="defn">
        <h3><span class="sw sw-orange" aria-hidden="true"></span>5× Outliers <small>default</small></h3>
        <p>The bar is <b>five times the profile's follower count</b>. It grows with the account, so it asks the same question of every creator: <i>which Reels reached far beyond their own audience?</i></p>
      </div>
      <div class="defn">
        <h3><span class="sw sw-plum" aria-hidden="true"></span>Min Views</h3>
        <p>The bar is <b>a number you choose</b>, from 1,000 to 1,000,000. It stays the same on every profile. It's useful when you only care about Reels past a mark like 100K.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <AccountCompare />

    <blockquote class="pull">
      <p><span class="smallcaps">Rule of thumb</span> Use <em>5×</em> to compare creators fairly, whatever their size. Use <em class="plum">Min Views</em> when you want one fixed bar across every profile.</p>
    </blockquote>
    <p class="aside-note">Either way, Outliers reads the follower count first. The Run button unlocks once it's loaded.</p>
  </div>
</section>
